{%- comment -%}
  ============================================================
  snippets/ak-notebook-badmusic.liquid
  BAD MUSIC — NOTEBOOK CONVERSION (Stage BM-1)
  (experiment theme 186464731416 only — DO NOT PUBLISH)

  The FIFTH notebook page (after Products, Life/Style, Club Hub,
  Narrative). Converts /pages/2025 (the Bad Music page → the
  TV-hero + cassette-shelf media page) to the notebook-paper system
  using the "scrapbook / taped media on notebook paper" direction —
  dark media modules stay dark ON the paper (the accepted Life/Style
  precedent, NOT a module reskin).

  - Rendered from ONE repurposed disabled spare custom_liquid slot in
    templates/page.badmusic.json (custom_liquid_RnLA6b — was a
    disabled fastbanner, position 3 right after ak-top so the class +
    paper render EARLY -> no flash of dark content) behind a LIQUID
    HANDLE GUARD: {% raw %}{% if page.handle == '2025' %}{% endraw %}.
  - Adds .ak-badmusic-page to <html> via the standard one-line
    classList hook (the established pattern; the ONLY JS here).
  - Paints the accepted legal-pad paper scoped to .ak-badmusic-page.
    The TV hero declares its own opaque #000 (overridden to transparent
    in Stage BM-1.1 — see below); #MainContent/.gradient/.shopify-section/
    .ak-top-wrap are forced transparent so the paper shows through
    everywhere (incl. the mobile top band).
  - Ports the accepted mask-PNG nav + ink header/cart/footer
    (Club Hub Phase 3.9 lineage, via the Products/Narrative port)
    re-scoped to .ak-badmusic-page; BAD (.ak-top-bad, the active tile
    on this route) reads purple #ff33ff + magenta glow at rest (the
    glow comes from base ak-top's .ak-top-bad.is-active .ak-top-bad-mask
    drop-shadow; this snippet only sets the colour to official #ff33ff).
  - Footer CTA adopts Due Date (Stage of the accepted footer-font lane;
    no '#' in the CTA -> no Tenada).
  - "BAD MUSIC" heading (custom_liquid_bm_heading) -> ink Due Date
    (its inline white/Impact/stroke/magenta-glow would be low-contrast
    on yellow); CONTENT + layout preserved.
  - Right "Coming Soon" cassette case (.ak-cas--soon .ak-cas__case has
    opacity:.72 -> turns muddy-olive over the yellow) is de-mudded to
    opacity:1; link/MP4/IntersectionObserver/geometry untouched.
  - Red banner (#akrb / custom_liquid_JpKeak): REMOVED in Stage BM-1.1
    (2026-06-15) by DISABLING the section in templates/page.badmusic.json
    ("disabled": true) — not CSS-hidden. The BM-1 "taped red marker
    strip" CSS for #akrb was dead afterward and has been deleted.
  - TV hero (#amerikid-tv-hero): BM-1.1 makes it sit on the paper
    (transparent bg, min-height:0, breathing padding, ink caption,
    subtle TV offset shadow) instead of a full-width #000 slab — see the
    STAGE BM-1.1 CORRECTION block below. The TV custom-liquid markup/JS
    is NOT edited (paint/spacing override only).
  - NO doodles in BM-1/BM-1.1 (separate Stage BM-2 after owner review).
  - NOT touched: sections/ak-top.liquid, sections/ak-footer.liquid,
    sections/ak-bm-album-link.liquid (cassette behaviour), the TV-hero
    custom-liquid MARKUP/JS (player/YouTube/scanlines/static — BM-1.1
    only overrides its background/min-height via page-scoped CSS, it does
    NOT edit the section), all other pages' snippets/templates.

  Revert (whole notebook host): in templates/page.badmusic.json set
  custom_liquid_RnLA6b back to "disabled": true with its original
  fastbanner liquid (or git checkout templates/page.badmusic.json), and
  delete this snippet.
  Revert BM-1.1 ONLY: remove "disabled": true from custom_liquid_JpKeak
  in templates/page.badmusic.json (the red banner returns) and delete the
  "STAGE BM-1.1 CORRECTION" CSS block in this snippet (the TV hero
  returns to its own #000 full-width slab).
  ============================================================
{%- endcomment -%}

<script>
  /* Page hook — this snippet only renders behind the page.handle == '2025'
     Liquid guard in templates/page.badmusic.json, so the class can be
     added unconditionally. */
  (function(){ document.documentElement.classList.add('ak-badmusic-page'); })();
</script>

{%- comment -%} ND-2A — render shared notebook mobile-drawer font (font-only; page-class-scoped; ak-top.liquid untouched) {%- endcomment -%}
{% render 'ak-notebook-drawer' %}

<style>
  /* ============================================================
     BAD MUSIC NOTEBOOK PAPER BACKDROP — CSS-only, scoped to
     .ak-badmusic-page. Same accepted values as the other notebook
     pages (shared --ak-paper-side-gap). html.ak-badmusic-page
     specificity is LOAD-BEARING: it must beat the global
     html,body{background:#000 !important} net in layout/theme.liquid.
     ============================================================ */
  html.ak-badmusic-page{
    --ak-paper-top-gap: clamp(150px, 17vw, 220px);    /* blank top band behind the KID logo */
    --ak-paper-bottom-gap: clamp(130px, 12vw, 190px); /* blank bottom band — ruled lines fade out so the page doesn't end mid-line */
    --ak-purple:#ff33ff;                              /* official AmeriKid purple (any var(--ak-purple) consumer, incl. base BAD active, resolves official) */
    background:#f5dd4f !important;                    /* overscroll/canvas fallback — beats the global html #000 via specificity */
  }
  html.ak-badmusic-page body{
    --ak-paper-side-gap: clamp(82px, 7vw, 128px);     /* shared inset for both vertical rules (red left + blue right) */
    background-color:#f5dd4f !important;              /* pale legal-pad yellow */
    background-image:
      linear-gradient(90deg,
        transparent calc(100% - var(--ak-paper-side-gap)),
        rgba(44,120,180,.60) calc(100% - var(--ak-paper-side-gap)),
        rgba(44,120,180,.60) calc(100% - var(--ak-paper-side-gap) + 2px),
        transparent calc(100% - var(--ak-paper-side-gap) + 2px)),   /* blue RIGHT margin rule */
      linear-gradient(90deg,
        transparent var(--ak-paper-side-gap),
        rgba(218,40,50,.74) var(--ak-paper-side-gap),
        rgba(218,40,50,.74) calc(var(--ak-paper-side-gap) + 2px),
        transparent calc(var(--ak-paper-side-gap) + 2px)),          /* red LEFT margin rule */
      linear-gradient(180deg,
        #f5dd4f 0,
        #f5dd4f var(--ak-paper-top-gap),
        transparent var(--ak-paper-top-gap)),                       /* blank yellow TOP band */
      linear-gradient(180deg,
        transparent calc(100% - var(--ak-paper-bottom-gap)),
        #f5dd4f calc(100% - var(--ak-paper-bottom-gap) + 36px)),     /* blank yellow BOTTOM band */
      repeating-linear-gradient(180deg,
        transparent 0 31px,
        rgba(44,120,180,.60) 31px 32px) !important;                 /* blue horizontal ruled lines */
    background-repeat:no-repeat, no-repeat, no-repeat, no-repeat, repeat !important;
    background-position:0 0, 0 0, 0 0, 0 0, 0 var(--ak-paper-top-gap) !important;
    background-attachment:scroll, scroll, scroll, scroll, scroll !important;
  }
  /* Transparency backstops so the body paper shows through the page chrome.
     .shopify-section + .ak-top-wrap are REQUIRED here (the Bad Music sections +
     the ak-top header wrapper carry opaque dark backgrounds — without these the
     top reads as a black band, esp. on mobile). The TV hero's own #000 band is
     overridden to transparent in the STAGE BM-1.1 CORRECTION block below, so the
     paper now shows through the TV section too (BM-1.1, 2026-06-15). */
  .ak-badmusic-page #MainContent{ background:transparent !important; }
  .ak-badmusic-page #MainContent .gradient{ background:transparent !important; background-image:none !important; }
  .ak-badmusic-page .shopify-section{ background:transparent !important; }

  /* ============================================================
     FONTS — Due Date display voice (duplicated scoped @font-face,
     the deliberate house pattern; same self-hosted asset as the
     other notebook pages). No Tenada: there is no '#' on this page.
     ============================================================ */
  @font-face{
    font-family: 'AK Due Date';
    src: url('{{ 'ak-due-date.woff2' | asset_url }}') format('woff2');
    font-weight: normal;
    font-style: normal;
    font-display: swap;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     HEADER / NAV / CART — FULL notebook parity, ported from the
     accepted treatment (Club Hub Phase 3.9 mask-PNG nav lineage)
     and re-scoped to .ak-badmusic-page. ak-top.liquid is NOT edited.
     BAD (.ak-top-bad) is the active tile on /pages/2025: it reads
     purple #ff33ff + magenta glow at rest (glow from base ak-top's
     .ak-top-bad.is-active .ak-top-bad-mask drop-shadow).
     ============================================================ */
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-wrap{ background:transparent !important; }
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-wrap::after{ background:none !important; }
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-label{ color:#15120b !important; }
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-bad{ color:#15120b !important; }
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-mobile-trigger{ color:#15120b !important; text-shadow:none !important; }
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-label::before,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-label::after{ opacity:0 !important; }
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-tile:hover .ak-top-label,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-tile.is-active .ak-top-label,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-bad:hover,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-bad.is-active,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-mobile-trigger:hover{ color:#ff33ff !important; }
  /* cart: black ink at rest, magenta glow on hover/focus; small right nudge so the blue right rule isn't crowded */
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-cart-container{ transform:translateX(clamp(4px, .6vw, 10px)) !important; }
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-cart-img{ filter:brightness(0) !important; }
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-cart-link:hover .ak-top-cart-img,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-cart-link:focus-visible .ak-top-cart-img{
    filter:brightness(0) drop-shadow(0 0 6px #ff33ff) drop-shadow(0 0 12px rgba(255,51,255,.5)) !important;
  }
  /* tighten logo->nav spacing + remove the dark-theme glow divider */
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-divider{ display:none !important; }
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-nav-panel{ padding-top:clamp(2px,0.6vw,8px) !important; }
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-nav-area{ margin-top:clamp(-22px,-2.2vw,-8px) !important; }
  /* per-tile mask + size + tilt (same PNGs / sizes / tilts as the accepted notebook nav) */
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-life{    --ak-nav-mask:url("https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0930/3267/7656/files/lifestyle_button.png?v=1780886497"); --ak-nav-png-size:clamp(260px, 21vw, 400px);   --ak-nav-tilt:-2.2deg; }
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-products{--ak-nav-mask:url("https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0930/3267/7656/files/products_button.png?v=1780886497");  --ak-nav-png-size:clamp(280px, 23vw, 430px);   --ak-nav-tilt:1.4deg; }
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-archive{ --ak-nav-mask:url("https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0930/3267/7656/files/archive_button.png?v=1780885375");   --ak-nav-png-size:clamp(270px, 22vw, 420px);   --ak-nav-tilt:-1.1deg; }
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-narrative{--ak-nav-mask:url("https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0930/3267/7656/files/narrative_button.png?v=1780885375"); --ak-nav-png-size:clamp(265px, 21.5vw, 410px); --ak-nav-tilt:1.8deg; }
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-contact{ --ak-nav-mask:url("https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0930/3267/7656/files/moniker_button.png?v=1780885375");   --ak-nav-png-size:clamp(220px, 18vw, 340px);   --ak-nav-tilt:-1.6deg; }
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-bad{ --ak-nav-tilt:-2.5deg; }
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-candy{ --ak-nav-tilt:1.2deg; }
  /* clickable tiles (all 7): no transform / bg-png / recolor-filter; transform excluded from transitions */
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-life,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-products,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-archive,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-narrative,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-contact,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-bad,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-candy{
    transform:none !important; -webkit-transform:none !important;
    background-image:none !important; filter:none !important;
    transition-property:filter, color, opacity, background-color !important;
    will-change:auto !important;
  }
  /* the five wordmark masks live on ::before (holds the static tilt; overrides base .ak-top-tile::before{display:none}) */
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-life::before,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-products::before,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-archive::before,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-narrative::before,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-contact::before{
    content:"" !important; display:block !important; position:absolute !important;
    left:50% !important; top:50% !important;
    width:var(--ak-nav-png-size) !important; height:var(--ak-nav-png-size) !important;
    transform:translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(var(--ak-nav-tilt)) translateZ(0) !important;
    -webkit-transform:translate(-50%, -50%) rotate(var(--ak-nav-tilt)) translateZ(0) !important;
    transform-origin:center center !important;
    backface-visibility:hidden !important; -webkit-backface-visibility:hidden !important;
    pointer-events:none !important;
    background-color:#15120b !important;
    -webkit-mask:var(--ak-nav-mask) center / contain no-repeat !important;
    mask:var(--ak-nav-mask) center / contain no-repeat !important;
    transition:background-color .12s ease, opacity .12s ease !important;
    z-index:1 !important;
  }
  /* hover / keyboard-focus / press -> the WHOLE wordmark turns purple (.is-active EXCLUDED — it has its own rule) */
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-life:hover::before, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-life:focus-visible::before, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-life:active::before,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-products:hover::before, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-products:focus-visible::before, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-products:active::before,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-archive:hover::before, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-archive:focus-visible::before, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-archive:active::before,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-narrative:hover::before, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-narrative:focus-visible::before, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-narrative:active::before,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-contact:hover::before, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-contact:focus-visible::before, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-contact:active::before{
    background-color:#ff33ff !important;
  }
  /* ACTIVE wordmark cue (only fires if a masked wordmark is the active tile; on
     /pages/2025 BAD is active — its ::before stays display:none, so this is a
     harmless no-op here, kept for parity / future-proofing). */
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-tile.is-active::before{
    background-color:#ff33ff !important;
    filter:
      drop-shadow(0 0 4px #ff33ff)
      drop-shadow(0 0 12px rgba(255,51,255,.75))
      drop-shadow(0 0 24px rgba(255,51,255,.5)) !important;
  }
  /* keep the five labels in the DOM for screen readers, but visually hidden in ALL states */
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-life .ak-top-label, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-life:hover .ak-top-label, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-life:focus-visible .ak-top-label, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-life:active .ak-top-label, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-life.is-active .ak-top-label,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-products .ak-top-label, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-products:hover .ak-top-label, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-products:focus-visible .ak-top-label, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-products:active .ak-top-label, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-products.is-active .ak-top-label,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-archive .ak-top-label, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-archive:hover .ak-top-label, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-archive:focus-visible .ak-top-label, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-archive:active .ak-top-label, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-archive.is-active .ak-top-label,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-narrative .ak-top-label, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-narrative:hover .ak-top-label, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-narrative:focus-visible .ak-top-label, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-narrative:active .ak-top-label, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-narrative.is-active .ak-top-label,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-contact .ak-top-label, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-contact:hover .ak-top-label, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-contact:focus-visible .ak-top-label, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-contact:active .ak-top-label, .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-contact.is-active .ak-top-label{
    color:transparent !important; text-shadow:none !important;
  }
  /* BAD / CANDY: tilt+scale on the inner graphic, anchor stays transform-stable (sizes BAD 1.18, CANDY 1.75) */
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-bad-mask{
    transform:scale(1.18) rotate(var(--ak-nav-tilt)) translateZ(0) !important;
    -webkit-transform:scale(1.18) rotate(var(--ak-nav-tilt)) translateZ(0) !important;
  }
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-top-candy-img{
    transform:scale(1.75) rotate(var(--ak-nav-tilt)) translateZ(0) !important;
    -webkit-transform:scale(1.75) rotate(var(--ak-nav-tilt)) translateZ(0) !important;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     FOOTER INTEGRATION — paper shows behind the footer, ink
     back-to-top, Due Date CTA. ak-footer.liquid is NOT edited.
     ============================================================ */
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-footer{ background:transparent !important; }
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-btt{ color:#15120b !important; }                     /* .ak-btt-text inherits */
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-footer-copy{ color:rgba(21,18,11,.5) !important; }
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-btt:hover .ak-btt-text,
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-btt:focus-visible .ak-btt-text{ color:#ff33ff !important; } /* preserve purple hover/focus */
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-footer-rule{ background:none !important; }           /* remove footer glow line (keep spacing) */
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-btt-text{ font-family:'AK Due Date', Impact, Haettenschweiler, 'Arial Narrow Bold', sans-serif !important; }

  /* ============================================================
     "BAD MUSIC" HEADING -> ink Due Date. The heading h2 carries
     INLINE styles (color:#fff, Impact, -webkit-text-stroke,
     magenta text-shadow) -> !important required to override inline.
     Content + size + layout preserved; only colour/font/stroke/glow
     change so it reads as ink on the yellow paper.
     ============================================================ */
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-bm-section-heading h2{
    color:#15120b !important;
    font-family:'AK Due Date', Impact, Haettenschweiler, 'Arial Narrow Bold', sans-serif !important;
    -webkit-text-stroke:0 !important;
    text-shadow:none !important;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     RIGHT "COMING SOON" CASSETTE CASE — de-mud. Base
     .ak-cas--soon .ak-cas__case is opacity:.72, so the dark case
     lets the yellow paper bleed through -> muddy olive. Force it
     opaque so it reads as a clean dark case on paper. ONLY the
     opacity changes — link/MP4/IntersectionObserver/geometry and the
     left "2025" album link are untouched. The "COMING SOON" overlay
     text + dimmed art-overlay still convey the teaser state.
     ============================================================ */
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-cas--soon .ak-cas__case{ opacity:1 !important; }

  /* ============================================================
     STAGE BM-1.1 CORRECTION (2026-06-15, owner feedback) — CSS-only,
     page-scoped. BM-1 passed QA but left two visual problems; this
     pass fixes both:

     (1) RED BANNER REMOVED. The moving red purchase banner
         (custom_liquid_JpKeak / #akrb) is now DISABLED at the template
         level in templates/page.badmusic.json ("disabled": true) — NOT
         CSS-hidden. The BM-1 '#akrb taped strip' rule is therefore dead
         code and has been deleted from this snippet. (Its CSS is
         recoverable from git history if the banner ever returns.)

     (2) TV HERO NO LONGER A FULL-WIDTH BLACK SLAB. The
         "2025 (The Album)" TV/player section (#amerikid-tv-hero) was a
         #000, ~100svh full-bleed band. It now sits ON the notebook
         paper: transparent background, content-driven height, vertical
         breathing room, ink caption, and a subtle hard offset paper
         shadow on the TV object. The ACTUAL TV/player is PRESERVED —
         .ak-tv and all of its markup/JS (player facade, YouTube,
         scanlines, static, play button, caption text) are untouched;
         only paint/spacing change here.

     HARD HAZARD — never add width / max-width / layout constraints to
     #amerikid-tv-hero, .ak-bg, .ak-stack, or .ak-tv, and never dispatch
     resize / rely on resize recompute: the TV's sizing/resize path can
     HANG THE RENDERER (Option A "constrain widths" was tried and
     rejected for exactly this). Only paint/spacing is touched here:
     background, min-height, padding, caption color, box-shadow,
     border-radius. The .ak-bg child is already transparent (not the
     problem); .ak-stage stays clamp(360px,96vw,1300px) and the hero's
     own overflow:hidden clips any shadow bleed -> no horizontal overflow.
     ============================================================ */
  .ak-badmusic-page #amerikid-tv-hero{
    background:transparent !important;
    min-height:0 !important;
    padding:clamp(24px,4vw,64px) 0 !important;
  }
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-caption{
    color:#15120b !important;
  }
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-tv{
    box-shadow:14px 14px 0 0 rgba(21,18,11,0.85) !important;
    border-radius:6px !important;
  }
  /* Mobile shadow safety — paint-only offset reduction so the hard
     offset shadow doesn't crowd the tight side gutter on small screens
     (.ak-stage is 96vw / 360px-min there). NO width/max-width touched. */
  @media (max-width:480px){
    .ak-badmusic-page .ak-tv{
      box-shadow:7px 7px 0 0 rgba(21,18,11,0.85) !important;
    }
  }

  /* ============================================================
     STAGE BM-TYPO-1 — typography polish (2026-06-15). CSS-only,
     font-family ONLY (no color/size/layout/spacing/markup change). The
     "2025 (The Album)" TV caption was inked in BM-1.1 but still rendered
     in Impact; switch it to the notebook Due Date voice so it matches
     the "BAD MUSIC" heading (already Due Date). No '#' in the caption ->
     no Tenada needed. The BM-1.1 ink colour (#15120b) is left untouched.
     ============================================================ */
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-caption{
    font-family:'AK Due Date', Impact, Haettenschweiler, 'Arial Black', sans-serif !important;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     STAGE BM-DOODLE-1 — mixtape margins (2026-06-15). Decorative ink
     doodle layer for /pages/2025 — "record-shop stickers in the paper
     margins". EXISTING ink assets only (hashtag/star/dollar/kid; the
     album's '#'-title motif + '$' + flair star + mascot). 5 marks, all
     in the OUTER paper gutters + top/footer bands — NEVER over the TV /
     YouTube / caption / BAD MUSIC heading / cassette shelf / album link /
     Coming Soon case / footer CTA / nav / cart. Decorative contract:
     aria-hidden (markup) + pointer-events:none + mix-blend-mode:multiply,
     PAGE-ANCHORED (absolute inside #MainContent{position:relative}, scrolls
     with the paper — NOT viewport-fixed), z-index:0 behind content (footer
     lifted to z-index:1). Right doodle sits LOW (bottom-anchored) so it
     never rests under the fixed top-right cart. Each mark is one
     self-contained rule; duplicate assets (hashtag ×2) are differentiated
     by placement/size/rotation. Revert = delete the
     <div class="ak-badmusic-doodles"> wrapper + this labeled block.
     ============================================================ */
  .ak-badmusic-page #MainContent{ position:relative; }              /* offset parent for the page-anchored layer */
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-footer{ position:relative; z-index:1; }     /* footer + CTA above the doodles */
  .ak-badmusic-page .ak-badmusic-doodles{
